  RISK click-pointerType-mouse — In iPadOS Safari a tap's click event carries pointerType "mouse" (Chrome's touch emulation reports "touch"). The studio's mesh onClick handlers (Baseplate, BrickObject, instanced bricks) read click.pointerType to ignore touch taps, so in Safari they see a mouse click; only the canvas-level touch click guard (450 ms after a touch pointerup) keeps a first tap from placing. It held for every tap of this run. Emulation hides this.
